From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:16:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 56/56] perf(canvas): a panel laid behind other frames is never
 live by distance

doop has no lightweight section, so a coloured panel with a title behind a group of screens is a
full document like any other. Such backdrops are large and nearly empty, and the live pick liked
them best: it takes the frames whose centre is nearest the view's, and a panel around the view
has its centre there. On a page of 47 screens on 22 nested panels (three deep, up to 10280x5790,
260 Mpx of canvas against the screens' 50), zooming to 60% booted the panels first; in headless
Chrome on a software GL the page took 1.7-2.3 s to show everything (0.7 s without the panels) and
3-5x the GPU-process time to zoom and pan.

backdrops.ts tells one by its place and its content together: it fully contains another document
frame (neither turned, canvas elements not counted), it is at least 1 Mpx and has at most 8
elements per Mpx of its area, and it is static (no script, video, canvas, nested document or
keyframes). On that page all 22 panels qualify (6-19 elements, at most 3.7 per Mpx) and no screen
does (61.5 per Mpx and up); on every page of a real instance (555 frames) nothing does, including
the two frames there that contain another (40 and 96 elements per Mpx). A backdrop shows its
picture at the level the view gives it; a press, a selection or an edit still pins it live.

On a copy of that page (production build, headless Chrome on a software GL, 1600x1000, off and
on alternating, median of 3; ratios count, not absolutes): zoom 8% -> 60% main thread 615 -> 313
ms, worst frame 324 -> 219 ms, live documents 7 -> 4; pan at 60% main thread 428 -> 183 ms, slow
frames 44 -> 24, GPU process 18.8 -> 12.8 s; zoom 60 > 95 > 60% slow frames 30 -> 4, GPU process
13.5 -> 3.7 s; pan away and back GPU process 13.4 -> 8.1 s. The fit jump (60% -> 8%) came out
worse, 89 -> 147 ms of main thread, within the run-to-run spread of that scenario.
localStorage['doop:backdrops'] = 'live' turns it off (read at load).
